LPA130
Render integration cannot represent a requested navigation feature.


LPA140
Quarto attempted execution before Ravel weaving.


LPA141
Org/Babel and Ravel both claim execution or tangling ownership.



An inferred ID (LPA102) is informational for an enabled heading declaration and a warning for a block-local declaration.



Each adapter needs fixtures for:

one piece and one fragment;
several fragments joined in source order;
visible display name distinct from semantic ID;
local and cross-document references with exact ranges;
a reference cycle and dependency path;
typed directives with no effects performed during parsing;
ignored/example blocks;
duplicate IDs and malformed attributes;
Unicode and entity/escape source mapping;
nested sections/containers;
included files, where supported;
a pipeline declared after the name and applied once after concatenation;
host-compatible versus pipe-extended Org/noweb spellings;
modern Markdown named fences interleaved with ambient unnamed fences;
LitPro H1-H4 peers, H5/H6 relative paths, repeated headings, and minors;
an equivalent Piece Document shared by all format fixtures.

Quarto adds golden renders for HTML and PDF showing:

visible piece captions;
working definition links;
uses and used by links;
a piece index;
an execution error mapped through a woven temporary cell.





