Should modern Markdown default to H2-H6 ambient ownership, or require a project to enable heading declarations explicitly?
Should markdown-litpro default to litpro-plus as proposed, or default to exact litpro-2017 and require opting into heading pipelines?
Is an inferred heading ID acceptable without a diagnostic in an explicitly selected legacy-style document?
Should #lp-main alone mark a named-fence declaration, or must .lp-piece always be present? Requiring the class is less magical.
